# .gitignore
# ==========
# Tells Git which files/folders to NEVER track, even if they exist in the
# project folder. Without this, `git add .` would try to commit thousands
# of virtual-environment files and compiled bytecode that don't belong in
# version control - they're either machine-specific, huge, or fully
# regenerable from other files that ARE tracked.

# The virtual environment: a self-contained copy of Python + installed
# packages, tied to THIS machine's OS/paths. Anyone cloning this repo
# recreates it themselves with `python -m venv .venv` + `pip install -r
# requirements.txt` - it should never be committed.
.venv/

# Python's compiled bytecode cache. Python creates these automatically
# next to any .py file it runs, purely as a speed optimization - they're
# regenerated automatically and are meaningless outside this exact machine.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# pytest's cache directory (created once we start writing tests) - same
# story: regenerable, machine-local, not meaningful history.
.pytest_cache/

# Environment variable files. Holds our real Anthropic API key (see
# app/config.py) - this file must NEVER be committed to Git, since Git
# history is effectively permanent and often gets pushed to a public or
# shared remote. (.env.example, the safe-to-commit template, is NOT
# listed here on purpose.)
.env

# (We used to have a SQLite database FILE listed here - kowshi.db. As of
# this update we use PostgreSQL instead (see app/database.py and
# app/config.py's DATABASE_URL) - conversation data now lives in a
# separate Postgres server process, not a file in this project folder at
# all, so there's nothing file-based left to ignore for it.)

# Node.js dependencies for the frontend build tooling (TypeScript,
# Tailwind CLI - see frontend/package.json). Same idea as .venv/: huge,
# machine-specific, and fully regenerable with `npm install` - never
# committed. (frontend/package-lock.json is DIFFERENT and NOT ignored -
# lockfiles pin exact versions and SHOULD be committed, the same way
# requirements.txt is, so everyone building this project gets identical
# dependency versions.)
frontend/node_modules/

# NOTE: compiled output in static/ (JS + CSS) is COMMITTED on purpose so Vercel
# can serve it without a Node build step. Re-run `npm run build` in frontend/
# and commit the result after changing frontend/src.
#
# (Originally ignored) Compiled frontend OUTPUT - generated from frontend/src/*.ts and
# frontend/src/input.css by `npm run build` (see frontend/package.json).
# static/index.html is hand-written SOURCE and stays tracked; these three
# are build artifacts that live in the same folder only because that's
# where FastAPI's StaticFiles mount already points - regenerate them any
# time with `npm run build` inside frontend/.

# Customer-uploaded approval documents (see app/config.py UPLOAD_DIR).
uploads/
